# DO NOT re-add `models/` here — it holds the trained weights.
#
# Locally, docker-compose bind-mounts ./ml:/app so the image copy is irrelevant.
# But on Render (Dockerfile build, no bind mount) the IMAGE is the only source
# of these files. Excluding models/ ships an ML container with NO trained
# weights — BehaveFormer/Siamese/CNN-LSTM silently fall back to RANDOM INIT.
# The trained weights (.pth/.json/.joblib, ~6MB) are git-tracked, so bake them in.
#
# `data/` (the 71MB PaySim CSV) IS excluded on purpose: if present, ensure_models.sh
# regenerates COPOD via train_fraud.py at boot, which OOMs the 512MB free tier
# (confirmed: "Out of memory (used over 512Mi)"). Without the CSV, COPOD regen is
# skipped and the container starts cleanly with the real behavioral weights loaded.
# Transaction-fraud (COPOD) stays disabled on free tier — acceptable; the biometric
# models are what matter. To enable it, use a >=2GB plan and drop this exclusion.
data/
reports/plots/

# Python caches / tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.venv-tools/
catboost_info/
datasets.tar.gz
citadel_train.zip